  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper studies two simulated, gate-based variational quantum classifiers under differential privacy: a 2-qubit 2D classifier and a 10-qubit binary MNIST classifier. For the 2D benchmarks, Table 2 reports accuracies of 1.00/0.98/0.98 on blobs, 0.87/0.91/0.87 on moons, and 0.97/0.88/0.86 on circles for non-private, ε=1.628, and ε=0.681 settings respectively; for MNIST, Table 3 shows the VQC reaches 0.98266667 at ε=1.07469683 and 0.96466667 at ε=0.40585425, while the classical NN is sometimes better at lower ε. The work is a proof-of-principle privacy-preserving QML study on classical simulators, not a demonstrated hardware quantum advantage result.",
